Searching for audio visual rental safety guidelines mostly turns up generic event planning checklists, tent securing, vendor vetting, weight capacity for structures, none of it specific to the AV equipment itself. What is missing almost everywhere, including from our own site until now, is the practical version: who is actually on site to react if something goes wrong, how a crew places a speaker or microphone stand so it does not become a hazard, and what a rental company honestly does and does not touch when it comes to overhead weight.

This page is that practical version, built around how Malaga Event Gear actually delivers a booking, not a generic list. [Contact us](/contact/) with your venue details if you want us to walk through your specific layout before you book.

