## How Far in Advance to Book

Every booking, and every change to one, needs at least 24 hours' notice. That window matters for safety planning too: telling us your venue's layout, power situation and expected guest flow ahead of time lets our crew plan stand placement and electrical load before arrival, rather than working it out on site while guests are already present. If your event has an unusual layout, multiple levels, or a venue you are not fully familiar with yourself, tell us as early as you can.

## Conclusion

Audio visual rental safety guidelines, for the equipment Malaga Event Gear actually supplies, come down to 4 honest practices: floor and stand based equipment only, with no overhead rigging or truss; careful stand placement out of walkways and doorways; venue power planned ahead of time rather than assumed; and, on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), a live technician who can react if something shifts during the event. [Contact us](/contact/) with your venue details, and for our full equipment range, see the [audio visual rental in Malaga guide](/blog/audio-visual-rental/).

## FAQs

### Does Malaga Event Gear use rigging or truss to mount speakers or lights overhead?

No. Every speaker, microphone and light we deliver is floor or stand mounted on its own tripod, confirmed against our own inventory. We do not stock or install overhead rigging or truss. See [What We Do Not Do: No Rigging or Overhead Truss](#what-we-do-not-do-no-rigging-or-overhead-truss) above.

### Who is actually on site to handle a safety issue during my event?

Only on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), which include a live technician who can reposition a stand, fix a loose cable, or react to a guest bumping equipment during the event. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) and [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) are self run after our crew installs and tests the system, so nobody is on site to react afterward. See [The Real Safety Difference](#the-real-safety-difference-a-technician-on-site-vs-a-self-run-setup) above.

### How do you keep guests safe around speaker stands and microphone stands?

Our crew places stands on level ground, out of primary walkways, and away from doorways, so guests are not walking through or around active equipment. On packages with a technician included, that person also watches for a stand getting nudged or a guest standing too close during the event itself. See [Guest Safety Around Equipment](#guest-safety-around-equipment) above.

### Does Malaga Event Gear check electrical load or circuit capacity before setup?

We do not publish a wattage or amperage spec sheet for our equipment, but we do ask about your venue's power situation when you book, how many outlets are near the setup area and whether they share a circuit, so our crew can plan the load ahead of time rather than improvising on site. See [Electrical Load and Circuit Safety](#electrical-load-and-circuit-safety) above.

### Are cables a safety risk at my event?

They can be if left loose across a walking path, which is exactly why our crew routes and secures cable, along walls and floor edges, taped flat wherever a run crosses a path, as part of every setup rather than leaving it as a separate concern.

### Does weather change how safely the equipment can be set up outdoors?

Yes, mainly around moisture near cabling and connectors, and wind affecting stand stability on grass, sand or an open terrace. We do not publish a weatherproof rating for any of our equipment, and on outdoor bookings we plan stand placement and cable routing around the actual conditions on the day rather than a fixed method regardless of weather.
